    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are leaning heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** today, who earns the highest score of the day (65.74) despite a challenging matchup against Shane McClanahan. Even with a -15% penalty from the platoon disadvantage, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from the park factor, making him our anchor. **Coby Mayo** also draws a strong start (61.44) in that same contest; while both players face a 34% rain risk, their raw production metrics remain high enough to warrant inclusion over safer, lower-ceiling options. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) and **Kyle Tucker** (58.24) represent our most stable outfield assets, with **Jackson Merrill** successfully navigating Dean Kremer\u2019s presence to provide high-leverage production, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a plug-and-play start regardless of the opposition.\n\nOur most difficult benching decision involved **Heliot Ramos**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 45.34 score. While **Heliot Ramos** benefited from a slight boost due to his ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries on the basepaths, his disadvantage against Dylan Cease proved too significant for the optimizer to overcome, pushing him behind the higher-upside profiles of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Andy Pages**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** (57.76), whose value is highly dependent on him securing a spot in the bottom of the order; should the official lineup shuffle him out, his status will drop significantly. Between the lingering rain concerns for our core trio and the constant volatility of \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, we are prepared to adjust our daily game caps to protect our long-term position in the 5x5 standings.",
